35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, the grant pays session fees for twelve months only, then the flat budget takes over. That timing is dangerous.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"- **Yumi**: @Ryuji, that timing is scary, but the real problem is that two wards lost their bus links entirely.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the ledger confirms it. The vehicle line overran by a third, while equipment closed under budget. The strain is in the recurring costs.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@May, the attendance sheets show forty visitors per session in the outer wards, beating our midweek numbers. We ignored that data before.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Daisuke, the register shows retired tradespeople running the repair clinic, but no one on payroll is trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, if the vehicle line overran, a mobile service is financially risky. I need to know if the grant covers that recurring cost.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, the bus links are gone, so a mobile service is the only way to reach those residents.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the grant covers session fees, not vehicle running. The ledger shows that line already overran. A mobile service would hit that same wall immediately.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Yumi, forty visitors per session proves demand, but the digitisation batch left half its images unindexed. We can’t just assume the next one will stick.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, the unindexed images worry me, but the real gap is supervision. We have the tradespeople, but no one trained to manage them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, if the vehicle line overran, a mobile service is financially risky. I need to know if the grant covers that recurring cost.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, the bus links are gone, so a mobile service is the only way to reach those residents.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, the grant covers session fees, not vehicle running. The ledger shows that line already overran. A mobile service would hit that same wall immediately.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, the unindexed images worry me, but the real gap is supervision. We have the tradespeople, but no one trained to manage them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I agree. The tradespeople are there, but without trained supervision, we risk repeating the same mistakes.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is a hard constraint. If the grant doesn’t cover running costs, the mobile option is financially unviable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, I hear the financial risk, but the bus links are gone. If we don't go to them, they simply disappear from our reach.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Yumi, the money is the problem, not the distance. If the vehicle line overran, we cannot fund a mobile service without breaking the budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@George, the vehicle line is a warning, but the attendance data proves the demand is real. We can't ignore the people we're already losing.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@George, the vehicle overrun is a hard constraint. If the grant doesn’t cover running costs, the mobile option is financially unviable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
